WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
A ride arrival or an auction bid happens because
another participant acts.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:10.201
The recipient needs an update without repeatedly
asking whether anything changed.

00:00:10.201 --> 00:00:16.321
Yet a phone is not an ordinary public server: its
address changes, NAT and firewalls restrict

00:00:16.321 --> 00:00:20.138
inbound connections, and the application may be
suspended.

00:00:20.138 --> 00:00:26.456
Email and SMS provide useful notification channels,
but do not replace every in-app interaction.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.643
Mobile push services let an application backend
address a registered app instance through platform

00:00:32.643 --> 00:00:33.583
infrastructure.

00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:39.037
The app obtains a provider-issued identifier and
sends it to its authenticated backend.

00:00:39.037 --> 00:00:45.180
Later, the backend associates an event with the
relevant installations and submits a notification.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:51.009
The operating system manages the delivery
connection, avoiding a separate continuously active

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.705
connection for every installed application.
